# Natural key vs surrogate key

## Two philosophies

- **Natural key** — from real data (`email`, `PAN`, `ISBN`, `SKU`) — **has meaning, can change**
- **Surrogate key** — system-generated int (`cust_wid = 1001`) — **no meaning, never changes**

## The problem — Anita changes her email

```
Natural key only        Surrogate key
#1  anita@old.com        1001  anita@old.com
#2  anita@new.com        1001  anita@new.com
= two customers?!        = one customer
```

- Stable surrogate → orders stay linked, and **SCD-2 history** becomes possible

## Best practice

- Warehouse dimension PK = **surrogate**; keep the **natural key as an attribute**
- Small int → **faster joins**, clean **multi-source** integration
